---
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
import HeroNetwork from "@components/diagrams/HeroNetwork.astro";
import {CURRENT_POSTS} from "@data/blog";
---
<Base title="VirtEngine — Open infrastructure. Shared possibility." description="A nonprofit-stewarded, open-source cloud marketplace protocol. Explore the research, understand the technology, and help develop public-benefit digital infrastructure.">
<section class="home-hero container-site">
<div class="hero-copy"><p class="kicker">OPEN SOURCE. PUBLIC BENEFIT.</p><h1>Open infrastructure.<br/><em>Shared possibility.</em></h1><p class="hero-lede">Our mission is to advance open education, privacy, and access to secure digital infrastructure.</p><p class="hero-body">VirtEngine is an open-source protocol stewarded by DETIO FOUNDATION LTD, an Australian not-for-profit public company limited by guarantee (ACN 699 651 771). We develop and document technology for transparent computing markets, verifiable identity, and privacy.</p><div class="action-row"><a class="button primary" href="/about">Discover our mission <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="/learn/how-the-marketplace-works">How VirtEngine works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><p class="hero-footnote">Open to study, build on, and improve. Apache 2.0 licensed.</p></div>
<figure class="network-plate"><div class="plate-top"><span>THE VIRTENGINE PROTOCOL</span><span class="plate-tag">IN DEVELOPMENT</span></div><div class="plate-heading">Many providers.<br/>One open protocol.</div><div class="network-art" role="img" aria-label="Tenants send orders and providers send bids to a shared network of validators. The protocol coordinates their agreement."><HeroNetwork /></div><figcaption><span>Request capacity</span><span>Verify &amp; coordinate</span><span>Provide resources</span></figcaption><div class="plate-bottom"><span>Designed for transparent participation</span><a href="/protocol" aria-label="Explore protocol architecture">↗</a></div></figure>
</section>
<div class="mission-band"><div class="container-site"><p>Technology held in public benefit.</p><span>Nonprofit stewardship</span><span>Open research &amp; education</span><span>Privacy &amp; access</span></div></div>
<section class="container-site home-section"><div class="section-intro"><div><p class="kicker">01 / WHY WE BUILD</p><h2>What we do.<br/>Who our work serves.</h2></div><p>We publish software, practical learning resources, and open specifications for students, researchers, developers, and infrastructure operators. Our work helps people understand, scrutinise, and contribute to the technology they may rely on.</p></div>
<div class="program-grid"><article><span class="card-number">01</span><h3>Learn in the open</h3><p>Original guides and module references explain how infrastructure markets work. Students, researchers, and developers can study the design and inspect its implementation.</p><a class="text-link" href="/learn">Explore the learning library →</a></article><article><span class="card-number">02</span><h3>Make infrastructure transparent</h3><p>The protocol describes how people request computing resources, how providers bid, and how usage is recorded. Open specifications make these decisions inspectable.</p><a class="text-link" href="/protocol">Understand the protocol →</a></article><article><span class="card-number">03</span><h3>Build trust with privacy</h3><p>VEID explores verifiable identity for network participation. It is decentralised protocol technology; the Foundation does not operate a central VEID verification service.</p><a class="text-link" href="/veid">Read about VEID →</a></article></div><p class="archive-note"><a href="/activities">Explore our activities, available resources, and intended public benefit →</a></p>
</section>
<section class="container-site status-block"><div><p class="kicker">DEVELOPMENT STATUS / 17 SEPTEMBER 2026</p><h2>Building openly.<br/>Launching carefully.</h2><p>The network is not live. You can read the source, review the design, and contribute today. Production services depend on testing and a separate launch approval.</p><a class="text-link" href="/network">Read the launch criteria →</a></div><ol class="launch-line"><li class="current"><span>NOW</span><h3>Research &amp; development</h3><p>Open code, documentation, and release preparation.</p></li><li><span>PLANNED · JAN 2027</span><h3>Public TestNet</h3><p>Validation with operators. Test state may reset.</p></li><li><span>PLANNED · MAR 2027</span><h3>MainNet, subject to approval</h3><p>Only after evidence, remediation, and a go/no-go decision.</p></li></ol></section>
<section class="container-site home-section"><div class="section-intro"><div><p class="kicker">02 / FIND YOUR WAY IN</p><h2>An open project.<br/>A place to contribute.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/participate">All ways to get involved ↗</a></div><div class="path-grid"><a href="/learn"><span>FOR CURIOUS MINDS</span><h3>Understand the technology</h3><p>Start with an accessible guide to the marketplace.</p><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a><a href="/participate#developers"><span>FOR DEVELOPERS</span><h3>Help improve the project</h3><p>Explore code, review documentation, and raise an issue.</p><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a><a href="/providers"><span>FOR INFRASTRUCTURE OPERATORS</span><h3>Prepare for participation</h3><p>Review requirements before a future test network.</p><b aria-hidden="true">↗</b></a></div></section>
<section class="container-site home-section journal-section"><div class="section-intro"><div><p class="kicker">03 / FROM THE JOURNAL</p><h2>The thinking behind the protocol.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href="/blog">Read all notes ↗</a></div><div class="journal-grid">{CURRENT_POSTS.slice(0,3).map((post,i)=><article><div class:list={["journal-cover",`cover-${i}`]}><span>FIELD NOTES / 0{i+1}</span><strong>{["An open\nmarketplace.","Trust in\nthe agreement.","Identity with\nprivacy."][i]}</strong><span>VIRTENGINE JOURNAL</span></div><p class="date">{new Date(post.publishedAt).toLocaleDateString('en-AU',{day:'numeric',month:'long',year:'numeric',timeZone:'UTC'})} · {post.readingTime}</p><h3><a href={`/blog/${post.slug}`}>{post.title} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h3><p>{post.description}</p></article>)}</div><p class="archive-note">Earlier work is preserved in the <a href="/blog/archive">2015–2016 historical archive</a>, separately from current technical guidance.</p></section>
<section class="container-site final-cta"><div><p class="kicker">LET’S BUILD SOMETHING USEFUL</p><h2>Public-benefit infrastructure<br/>starts with participation.</h2></div><a class="button primary" href="/contact">Talk to the Foundation ↗</a></section>
</Base>